seg-88c3cc6c3800 = Every score is modelled unless a row says an external oracle agreed. Licence of the specification and manifests: CC-BY-4.0 / CC0 proposed, owner decision pending. The real-data holdout is not secret: see the specification, section { "4" }.

# attr:aria-label
seg-68e7ed4fc6ee = What a row may say

# text
seg-7912ad415e48 = What a row means

# text
seg-7b6aa7dbc2e4 = A score describes a log, not a product.

# text
seg-69cc3c1470b3 = A row says: this file scored X on split S under specification version V. It does not say a product is certified, conformant, approved or endorsed, and no organisation is named as an endorser.

# text
seg-dd289a4fc50a = The data are recorded or synthetic and named in the specification. Third-party data is never copied into the repository: manifests and fetch scripts pin each file by SHA-256, and each licence is recorded before the data is used.

# text
seg-d48b2ec4cbe8 = The truth for a recorded log is the test plan's scheduled slots, not recorded on-air times, so a detection probability is a lower bound. The specification says so beside each task.

# text
seg-6883a66f3bdd = A sealed holdout is scored only in a leaderboard round, and its seed is revealed after it. Bars for any baseline that claims a number are committed before the scored run and never loosened afterwards; a miss is recorded as NOT MET.

# text
seg-97d14f361df5 = Verdicts as recorded in the results file: the scorer bars, C1 to C3 and D2 are met; A2 is NOT MET (agc_k_sigma AUC { "0.766" } against at least { "0.80" } on the test split), D1 is NOT MET (largest gap { "0.0301" }) and task (b) R1 is NOT MET (carried, not re-run). No bar is loosened.

# text
seg-23023a10ef10 = Advisory only: Kshana results are modelled or measured against stated references, not an approval or a statement of conformance.

